</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Denike</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Certainty, uncertainty, and the spatiality of disease: a West Nile virus example. Jour</article-title><source>Stochast Environ Res Risk Assess</source><year>2007</year><volume>21</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>523</fpage><lpage>31</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="FDN023C32"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>McMichael</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Meng</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Spatial dynamics of a SARS epidemic in an urban area</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>2006</year><volume>84</volume><fpage>965</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17242832</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="FDN023C33"><label>33</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meng</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Understanding the spatial diffusion process of severe acute respiratory syndrome in Beijing</article-title><source>J Public Health</source><year>2005</year><volume>119</volume><fpage>1080</fpage><lpage>7</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="FDN023C34"><label>34</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mikler</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Venkatachalam</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramisetty-Mikler</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decisions under uncertainty: a computational framework for quantification of policies addr